                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8b6fe849-b3ca-334b-abb9-27c78fff1cc1",
                        "entry_id": "fc0970a6-f5be-3c96-abf9-94d3c8bdefed",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A woodpecker."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Appalachia",
                            "Southern-US",
                            "slang"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "906069a5-884c-4f92-b85a-236bbd84db76",
                                "sense_id": "8b6fe849-b3ca-334b-abb9-27c78fff1cc1",
                                "text": "On the morning of the next, one of Mr. White's daughters came into the house to inform me that there was a \"peckerwood\" in a tree in the yard. I immediately took my gun and went out to investigate thinking that perhaps it was a Pileolated Woodpecker, a bird I wanted to obtain."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8cbba52c-4659-41ef-8214-1556d2faeb46",
                                "sense_id": "8b6fe849-b3ca-334b-abb9-27c78fff1cc1",
                                "text": "When I was a boy, I rooted over an old dead sourwood to get some peckerwood eggs."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "50005865-55cc-45e3-99b6-4d7c58a61ffc",
                                "sense_id": "8b6fe849-b3ca-334b-abb9-27c78fff1cc1",
                                "text": "There was nothing but a peckerwood on an oak tree."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "27ad9581-648d-3946-877a-e3afc590605b",
                        "entry_id": "fc0970a6-f5be-3c96-abf9-94d3c8bdefed",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A peckerwood sawmill."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Appalachia",
                            "Southern-US"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "19817f39-c041-4e5a-a169-a96e5817bbec",
                                "sense_id": "27ad9581-648d-3946-877a-e3afc590605b",
                                "text": "Throughout this territory are mills of every variety and size, from the small \"peckerwood\" tractor mill capable of cutting only a few thousand feet of lumber per day to the world's largest pine lumber mill with a capacity of more than one million feet per day."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9254bff2-5dcc-4435-bd20-09dfb97de175",
                                "sense_id": "27ad9581-648d-3946-877a-e3afc590605b",
                                "text": "The Langdale Company's new centralized sawmill and debarker in 1958 constituted a tremendous advance over the old peckerwood technology."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ea4c8f76-2e68-39ea-9ea2-56aa6c5d7878",
                        "entry_id": "fc0970a6-f5be-3c96-abf9-94d3c8bdefed",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A white person, especially a Southerner, or one who is ignorant, rustic, or bigoted."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "US",
                            "ethnic",
                            "offensive",
                            "slang",
                            "slur"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "cb477261-4427-472c-a99b-32dc741f5a3e",
                                "sense_id": "ea4c8f76-2e68-39ea-9ea2-56aa6c5d7878",
                                "text": "All the time I was stretched out on the infirmary cot I kept looking at the blank walls and seeing the mean, murdering faces of those Southern peckerwoods when they went after Big Six and the others with their knives."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "716a89fe-e2c5-48c7-b098-fc5df0586c32",
                                "sense_id": "ea4c8f76-2e68-39ea-9ea2-56aa6c5d7878",
                                "text": "Just as prejudiced as a Mississippi peckerwood when it comes to colored people."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "115feba4-b141-3e1a-9f6b-4e7c74c8e557",
                        "entry_id": "fc0970a6-f5be-3c96-abf9-94d3c8bdefed",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A white (male) inmate, especially one who is racist or who is a member of a race-based prison gang."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "slang"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    }
